From eed9ba583ad1ac5cf30ac5ad9664019a076778e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:11:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Telegram: Build with MinGW-w64

* Generate the toast activation headers and IIDs with widl, which
  mingw-w64 provides in place of midl.

* /PDBPAGESIZE is an MSVC linker option.

* MSVC embeds Telegram.manifest at link time, with MinGW it has to come
  from the resource script. It replaces the generic manifest MinGW links
  in by default, so the UTF-8 code page and DPI awareness settings apply.

* GCC has no SEH __try/__except: call the cleanup helpers directly, they
  catch C++ exceptions themselves.

* __uuidof(ToastActivator) needs the IID declared with __CRT_UUID_DECL,
  GCC ignores DECLSPEC_UUID.

* PropVariantToCLSID() is an inline wrapper of PropVariantToGUID() in the
  Windows SDK that mingw-w64 lacks; call the latter. Also define
  APPUSERMODEL_STARTPINOPTION_NOPINONINSTALL, missing from <propkey.h>.

* MSYS2's C++/WinRT projection is generated from Windows metadata that
  predates the window-owned KeyCredential overloads of Windows 11 24H2,
  so take the unowned path the code already has for older systems.

* GCC rejects '?:' between two different rpl::producer types.
